# Everything the running service has no use for. Keeps the image small and, more to the
# point, keeps things that should never leave this machine out of it.
#
# This file has to sit at the REPO ROOT, because Docker reads .dockerignore from the
# build context and the context is the repo root (see render.yaml). Patterns are matched
# from there, and a bare `test/` would only ever match a top-level test/ — which is why
# every path below names its app explicitly rather than relying on a pattern to reach
# down into both.

# Secrets and local state
scrapbook/.env
scrapbook/bot/.offset
scrapbook/pb_data/

# The local PocketBase binary — the image fetches its own, for linux
scrapbook/pocketbase/

# Development only
scrapbook/test/
scrapbook/tools/
scrapbook/bot/
scrapbook/preview.html
scrapbook/serve.py
scrapbook/data/
gallery/test/
gallery/tools/
gallery/preview.html
gallery/serve.py

# NOTE: gallery/data/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It looks like scrapbook/data/ above,
# but it is the opposite thing: scrapbook/data/mock.json is a no-backend fixture, while
# gallery/data/artworks.json IS the collection and the gallery is empty without it.

**/node_modules/
.git/
.github/
**/.claude/

# Documentation. Needs the glob: a bare *.md only matches the root.
**/*.md

# Large sample media, dropped in by hand for the preview bench
scrapbook/assets/sample-clip.*

# The icon master. Kept in git so the sizes can be regenerated, but 2 MB of it has no
# business in the image when every size actually served is derived from it.
scrapbook/assets/icon-source.png

**/.DS_Store
